        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 68-year-old male, who presented on 12/10/2013 with worsening dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced exercise tolerance consistent with an acute exacerbation of his known COPD. On admission, clinical examination revealed bilateral expiratory wheeze and reduced air entry. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis demonstrated mild hypoxaemia with no significant hypercapnia. Blood tests showed a modest inflammatory response. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, controlled oxygen therapy, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout his stay. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 13/10/2013 with a course of oral prednisolone and optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. I remain available for any queries.</div>"
            },
